{"Your turn": "B001", "What are we shaping next?": "B002", "Tell us what you have in mind. It can be a clear brief or just the start of an idea. We’ll help shape the next steps and keep everything simple from there.": "B003", "Start a Project": "B004", "Need Help": "B005", "Not sure which service you need?": "B006", "Tell us the problem, not the deliverable. We’ll tell you what the work actually needs and come back with a clear scope, a timeline and a price. No obligation.": "B007", "Request Assistance": "B008", "Next Step": "B009", "Ready to build a brand people remember?": "B010", "Tell us where the brand is today and what it needs to do next. We’ll come back with a clear scope, a timeline and a price. No obligation.": "B011", "Ready to get the message right?": "B012", "Tell us who you need to reach and what you need them to do. We’ll come back with a clear scope, a timeline and a price. No obligation.": "B013", "Ready to put it on camera?": "B014", "Tell us what you need to shoot and where it needs to run. We’ll come back with a clear scope, a timeline and a price. No obligation.": "B015", "Build": "C001", "We do many things very well.": "C002", "View All Work": "C003", "Selected Works": "C004", "See All": "C005", "Trusted by the ambitious": "C006", "What We Do": "C007", "Start a": "C008", "Project": "C009", "We live in the details. The pixels, the strategy, the timing. If you're building something real, we'll meet you there.": "C010", "Let's Chat": "C011", "Frames that hold the eye. Films that carry the feeling. Every shot, cut, and grade shaped with a clear creative point.": "C012", "Comms": "C013", "Strategy, content, and distribution, orchestrated to reach the right audience at the right moment.": "C014", "Visual Identity": "C015", "Packaging Design": "C016", "Creative Advertising": "C017", "Brand Strategy": "C018", "Logo Design": "C019", "Brand Guidelines": "C020", "Photography": "C021", "Videography": "C022", "Post-Production": "C023", "Color Grading": "C024", "Communications": "C025", "Social Media": "C026", "Digital Marketing": "C027", "Public Relations": "C028", "Content Strategy": "C029", "Campaign Management": "C030", "No egos": "C031", "Strategists, designers, filmmakers, and communicators who care about the work as much as you do. No egos, just craft and conviction.": "C032", "Meet the People": "C033", "The Diary": "C034", "What are you waiting for?": "C035", "Why your brand needs a point of view": "C036", "The death of safe design": "C037", "Motion is the new typography": "C038", "Campaigns that outlive the algorithm": "C039", "Playing it safe is the riskiest move in a crowded market. We break down why bold creative consistently outperforms the forgettable.": "C040", "Static brands are invisible brands. How motion design became the most important layer of modern identity systems.": "C041", "Social platforms change daily. We build communication strategies anchored to human truths, not trending formats.": "C042", "Team members coming soon.": "C043", "People": "C044", "Two earthquakes": "C045", "Est. 2019, Tirana, Albania": "C046", "The ground shook twice. The world shut down. And somewhere in the middle of all of that, two 22-year-olds decided it was a good time to build an agency.": "C047", "Our motto": "C048", "It means we do not stand at the bottom and point to the peak. We climb with you. We enter the work fully. The meetings, the pressure, the decisions, the parts no one sees. We learn how your business moves before we decide how your brand should move.": "C049", "We do not disappear after the delivery. We stay close, challenge what needs to be challenged, and take responsibility for the path we recommend. Because real partnership is not agreement at every step. It is trust, honesty, endurance, and the will to reach the top together.": "C050", "“We've been told we're too involved.”": "C051", "We consider that a compliment.": "C052", "The equation": "C053", "BoldCrest began where two different strengths met. Xhulio brought the visual discipline, the instinct for form, and the ability to turn ideas into images with character. Aldo brought the relationships, the conversations, and the trust needed to turn one project into a long-term partnership.": "C054", "The team": "C055", "Something slightly off, slightly unusual, slightly theirs. And that's exactly what makes them belong here. We are different people who are somehow made of the same thing.": "C056", "We bully each other. We cook together. We have traditions that make no sense to anyone outside this room. And when someone is sick, we show up.": "C057", "It is, honestly, harder to find someone who won't disturb our peace than someone who has a great portfolio.": "C058", "The work": "C059", "The best thing we can do is make something bigger than ourselves, then step back and watch it belong to the world.": "C060", "That's why we exist.": "C061", "Before you go": "C062", "A small warmth. A little confidence. Maybe a smile at the chaos of two kids building something real in a country still figuring out what “brand” means.": "C063", "Want to join our team?": "C064", "Visit Careers": "C065", "BoldCrest team": "C066", "Climbing Mountains Together.": "C067", "Xhulio and Aldo, founders of BoldCrest": "C068", "Every person has a glitch in their system.": "C069", "Diary": "C070", "The Latest": "C071", "From Our": "C072", "World": "C073", "Read deeper into what we do, think, and create at BoldCrest.": "C074", "No posts yet. Check back soon.": "C075", "Services": "C076", "Company": "C077", "Contact": "C078", "Talk to us or ask us anything.": "C079", "Contact Us": "C080", "Social": "C081", "Legal": "C082", "Privacy Notice": "C083", "Cookie Policy": "C084", "Communication": "C085", "All Services": "C086", "Work": "C087", "Back to top": "C088", "Start with a Hello": "C089", "We'll take it from there": "C090", "Let's Talk. It doesn't matter how big your business is or weird your questions are, they're worth asking, and we will get back to you shortly.": "C091", "Email": "C092", "Location": "C093", "Follow Us": "C094", "Other": "C095", "Email address": "C096", "Send another message": "C097", "I’m Megi.": "C098", "I’m looking for": "C099", "In a sentence or two, what are you trying to build?": "C100", "I want to…": "C101", "Got it.": "C102", "When would you like to kick this off?": "C103", "We can start": "C104", "And when do you want it live?": "C105", "I’m aiming for": "C106", "What budget range did you have in mind?": "C107", "I’d say": "C108", "What’s the best email to reach you on?": "C109", "One last thing before we go.": "C110", "I found you through": "C111", "Sending…": "C112", "That’s everything, message received.": "C113", "We’ll get back to you at": "C114", "Packaging design": "C115", "TV commercials": "C116", "Social media": "C117", "ASAP, within the next two weeks.": "C118", "Soon, next month would be great.": "C119", "Within the next 3 months.": "C120", "No rush. Whenever fits your team.": "C121", "Within 3 months.": "C122", "Within 6 months.": "C123", "In about a year.": "C124", "Open-ended, quality over speed.": "C125", "Under €5,000": "C126", "A client referral": "C127", "A friend or colleague": "C128", "Somewhere else": "C129", "Something went wrong — please try again.": "C130", "Reach me at": "C131", "One cookie a day ?": "C132", "Keeps the glitches away.": "C133", "Accept": "C134", "Deny": "C135", "Cookie consent": "C136", "Error": "C137", "Let's get you": "C138", "The page you were looking for doesn't exist, or it's moved.": "C139", "But there's plenty more to see, head back and take a look.": "C140", "Page Not Found": "C141", "Back to Home": "C142", "We craft brands": "E001", "and tell stories": "E002", "that don't just inform.": "E003", "They pull people in.": "E004", "Disciplines": "E005", "Process": "E006", "How every BoldCrest project works": "E007", "We take what your brand is, what it wants to become, and how people should remember it, then turn that into an identity people can recognize, trust, and return to.": "E008", "A great brand in silence is a waste. We put yours where it belongs, in front of the right people, saying the right thing, at the right moment.": "E009", "Discovery & Brief — We listen before we create. Deep immersion into your brand, audience, competitors, and goals to build a brief worth building from.": "E010", "Strategy & Direction — Insights become a strategic foundation, positioning, messaging hierarchy, creative direction, and a clear plan of action.": "E011", "Creative Development — Concepts, iterations, and refinement. We present, collaborate, and push until the work is something we're both proud of.": "E012", "Production & Delivery — Pixel-perfect execution across every deliverable. Print, digital, motion, everything ships production-ready, on time.": "E013", "Ongoing Partnership — Great brands evolve. We stay close to help you adapt, grow, and keep the work as sharp as the day it launched.": "E014", "What types of businesses do you work with?": "E015", "If it can be launched, booked, tasted, worn, visited, financed, or experienced, we can help people understand it, want it, and choose it. We work with brands across food & beverage, fashion, hospitality, real estate, healthcare, finance, and tech. From startups building their first identity to established brands growing through multi-channel campaigns.": "E016", "Can I hire BoldCrest for just one thing, or do I need a full package?": "E017", "You can start with one thing. We just can't promise you'll want to stop there. We do one time projects like a brand identity, a photoshoot, or a campaign kit, as well as ongoing retainers that cover content planning, production, and management. The setup depends on what your brand needs now and how far you want to take it next.": "E018", "What makes you different from other agencies?": "E019", "We connect the dots others usually separate. Our decisions are shaped by real project data, not guesswork. Our team works fully in house, from design and copy to photography, video, and animation. Strategy and execution move together from the very first step. The people who think are the people who make.": "E020", "Do you work with international brands?": "E021", "Yes. We work with brands across different markets through clear communication, structured timelines, and a process built to keep every project aligned from start to finish. Some of our collaborations include Magniflex, Fentimans, Red Bull, Coca Cola, Fanta, Tomarchio, Piaggio Group, Wolt, and Cipriani.": "E022", "How do I start a project?": "E023", "Hit \"Start a Project\" and fill out the brief. Or email info@boldcrest.com. We'll schedule a discovery call, understand your needs, and come back with a tailored proposal.": "E024", "How do revisions and feedback work?": "E025", "Every service includes defined revision rounds (typically 2). If we made the error, we fix it free, no questions. If you change direction after approval, additional rounds are available at transparent rates. Clear, fair, documented.": "E026", "Brand Systems That Clarify Who You Are and Amplify How You're Seen": "E027", "Your brand is the promise you make before you say a word. We build identity systems, logos, visual languages, packaging, guidelines, and campaigns, that earn trust on sight and hold up everywhere your name appears.": "E028", "Start Your Brand Project": "E029", "What Strong Brand Development Does for Your Business?": "E030", "Our Brand Development Capabilities": "E031", "How We Build Brand Identity Systems": "E032", "What Sets Our Brand Development Apart": "E033", "Instant Recognition — A well built identity makes your brand recognizable across every touchpoint, from a storefront sign to a 1 inch social avatar. We design identity frameworks that work at every scale, keeping your brand consistent, distinctive, and easy to recognize wherever it appears.": "E034", "Trust Before the First Conversation — Professional branding signals credibility. When your visual identity is cohesive and intentional, customers trust you before they've spoken to you.": "E035", "Competitive Separation — In a crowded market, attention goes to the brands that know exactly who they are. A distinctive identity gives you the edge, helping your brand become easier to recognize, harder to replace, and impossible to mistake for the next name in line.": "E036", "Visual Identity — We build your full visual identity to give your brand a presence people notice now and remember long after. From logo, color palette, typography hierarchy, graphic patterns, iconography, and photographic style direction, we explore every detail to define the right visual language for your brand. Every element is created to feel cohesive, distinctive, and ready to work across every medium.": "E037", "Logo Design — Your logo is the single most visible element of your brand. We develop a strategically grounded concept that feels distinctive, balanced, and built to stand the test of time. Through collaborative refinement, every curve, letterform, and detail is shaped until the logo feels not just designed, but meant to exist.": "E038", "Brand Guidelines — The rulebook that keeps your brand consistent when you're not in the room. Our brand books document every element with do's and don'ts and real application examples. From 30-page essentials to 80-page comprehensive manuals.": "E039", "Brand Strategy — Before any visual work begins, we define who you are, who you're for, and where you stand in the market. Audience mapping, competitive analysis, positioning territory, and brand architecture.": "E040", "Packaging Design — The shelf is your stage. We design packaging that tells your story at the point of decision, from single products to full line systems with variant logic, 3D mockups, and print-ready die lines.": "E041", "Creative Advertising — From key visuals and campaign concepts to event materials, ATL rollouts, print, digital, outdoor, and beyond, we create advertising systems built to travel across channels. Our work is shaped to be visually distinctive and strategically written, so every campaign has both the look to capture attention and the message to stay with people.": "E042", "Discovery & Research — A deep-dive workshop into your business goals, audience, competitive landscape, and brand aspirations. Not a questionnaire, a strategic conversation that shapes everything.": "E043", "Moodboard & Direction — We present curated visual territories exploring different directions for your brand's look and feel. You choose the territory, and we align before any design begins.": "E044", "Concept Development — One concept, fully resolved. We don't hedge with variations, we commit to a single direction grounded in strategy and present it with the rationale behind every choice, so you understand why it works, not just how it looks.": "E045", "Refinement & Feedback — Structured revision rounds refine the chosen direction until every detail is right. We welcome honest feedback and push back when we believe a different path serves you better.": "E046", "Brand System Delivery — Comprehensive brandbook, final files in all formats, and a brand toolkit ready for implementation. Logo, identity, packaging, guidelines. Everything documented and production-ready.": "E047", "Implementation & Support — We roll out the brand across your touchpoints: stationery, social templates, signage, packaging production files. And we stay available for ongoing brand evolution as you grow.": "E048", "Strategy Before Style — We never open Illustrator before the brief is locked. Every design choice has to answer to the brand, the market, and the brief, not to whatever is trending this quarter.": "E049", "Designed to Scale — Whether you are a neighborhood cafe or a national FMCG brand, your identity needs to look just as strong on a coffee cup as it does across a full packaging line, campaign rollout, or city billboard.": "E050", "Full Creative Team — Senior designers, copywriters, and creative directors collaborate on every project. You are not getting one person's point of view. You are getting a room full of people who know how to make brands look sharper, sound clearer, and land exactly where they should.": "E051", "Proven Track Record — 300+ projects across 11 industries means we do not walk into brand challenges guessing. We bring tested processes, project data, and the kind of experience that helps brands move from creative ideas to creative decisions that actually hold up.": "E052", "Packaging Expertise Built In — Unlike agencies that outsource packaging, we have specialized packaging craft in house. Identity and packaging are shaped by the same team, so the brand feels consistent from the first logo application to the final shelf presence.": "E053", "Clear Revision Policy — 2 rounds included on brand development. If the error is on our side, we correct it at no additional cost. If the direction changes after sign off, additional rounds are available at transparent rates.": "E054", "Still & Motion — Frames and footage that hold attention.": "E055", "Communication — Strategy and distribution that reach the right people.": "E056", "What's the difference between a logo and a visual identity?": "E057", "A logo is one element, your mark. A visual identity is the complete system: logo, colors, typography, patterns, imagery style, and the rules governing how they work together. Think of the logo as your face and the identity as your entire wardrobe, posture, and voice.": "E058", "How many logo concepts will I see?": "E059", "One. Not because we limit the process, but because we believe the strongest direction should not arrive as a guessing game. Before we present, we explore, compare, and refine internally until the concept answers the brief, reflects the brand vision, and has a clear reason to exist. From there, we develop the chosen direction through 2 to 3 collaborative revision rounds.": "E060", "Can you rebrand an existing business?": "E061", "Absolutely. We have handled rebrands for Tepelene, Infratech, Hako, Tierr, Baboon, Albita, and other established brands. Our process starts with a clear brand audit, then moves into logo refinement, updated visual assets, brand templates, and a complete guide that helps the new identity work consistently across every touchpoint.": "E062", "Do I own the final brand files?": "E063", "Yes. Full ownership transfers on final payment. All source files (AI, SVG, PNG, PDF) plus the brand book. We retain portfolio rights unless otherwise agreed.": "E064", "Can you design packaging as part of a branding project?": "E065", "Yes, and it often makes the brand stronger. Packaging is where identity becomes something people can hold, notice, and choose. We design everything from single product packs to full product lines, making sure the brand looks clear, consistent, and shelf ready from the first SKU to the last.": "E066", "How long does a branding project take?": "E067", "Logo: 2-3 weeks. Full visual identity with brandbook: 4-8 weeks. Packaging: 2-4 weeks per product. We'll lock a timeline in our first meeting.": "E068", "Strategy, Content, and Distribution. Orchestrated to Reach the Right People.": "E069", "A great brand in silence is a waste. We put yours where it belongs, in front of the right audience, saying the right thing, at the right moment. From monthly social management to full-scale campaign orchestration.": "E070", "Start a Communication Project": "E071", "What Strategic Communication Delivers?": "E072", "Our Communication Capabilities": "E073", "How We Run Communication": "E074", "Why Brands Choose BoldCrest for Communication": "E075", "Consistent Visibility — Your audience scrolls every day. A structured content system keeps your brand visible, relevant, and top-of-mind, without you writing captions at midnight.": "E076", "Strategic Reach, Not Random Noise — Every post, campaign, and media placement connects to a plan. We build calendars tied to business goals, seasonal opportunities, and audience behavior.": "E077", "Measurable Growth — Monthly reporting with KPIs, engagement metrics, audience growth, and competitor benchmarking. You'll know exactly what's working and what to adjust.": "E078", "Social Media Management — End-to-end social media: content planning, calendar creation, copywriting, design coordination, scheduling, and performance reporting. Four tiers from 9 to 20 posts/month.": "E079", "Digital Marketing — Paid campaigns across Meta, Google, and other platforms. Strategy, audience targeting, creative development, pixel setup, A/B testing, and ongoing optimization.": "E080", "Content Strategy — We define content pillars, audience segments, posting cadence, platform strategy, and seasonal calendars. A living system we operate month after month.": "E081", "Campaign Management — Full campaign orchestration from concept to execution: brief development, creative production, media planning, channel coordination, and performance tracking.": "E082", "Public Relations — Press outreach, influencer coordination, event PR, and brand reputation management. Amplify your message beyond owned channels.": "E083", "Media Planning — Channel selection, budget allocation, and timing optimization across paid, owned, and earned media. Maximizing reach while respecting your budget.": "E084", "Audit & Onboarding — We review your current presence, audit existing content, analyze competitors, and identify gaps. A clear picture of where you stand before we touch a single channel.": "E085", "Strategy & Calendar — Monthly content calendars tied to business goals, seasonal moments, and audience behavior. Every post has a purpose: awareness, engagement, conversion, or community.": "E086", "Content Production — Posts are designed, reels edited, animations crafted, and copy written. Everything runs through internal review. Coordinated with our Still & Motion team.": "E087", "Approval & Scheduling — You review, provide consolidated feedback (one contact person, 48-hour window), and we schedule everything. Your feed runs on autopilot.": "E088", "Campaign Execution — Paid campaigns launched, monitored, and optimized in real time. A/B testing, audience refinement, and creative rotation to maximize performance.": "E089", "Reporting & Optimization — Monthly performance reports: what worked, what to improve, what to try next. Strategy adjusts based on real data, not gut feeling.": "E090", "Production + Distribution Under One Roof — Most agencies either create content or manage channels. We do both. The people planning your calendar are the same people shooting your content.": "E091", "22+ Brands in Active Management — Not a side service, our most active discipline. From boutique fashion accounts to national FMCG campaigns.": "E092", "Data-Backed Pricing — Every price is built from real project data, not industry guesswork. You know exactly what you're paying for.": "E093", "Dedicated Account Manager — Every client gets a named contact who knows your brand, schedule, and preferences. No revolving door.": "E094", "Scalable from Starter to Full-Service — Start with 9 posts/month and scale to 20+ with photography, video, animation, and ads layered on.": "E095", "Transparent Revision Policy — 1 revision per post, 48-hour window. Monthly plans get 2 rounds. If we made the mistake, the fix is free.": "E096", "Brand Development — Identity systems that clarify who you are.": "E097", "How many posts do I get per month?": "E098", "Base packages range from 9 (Scout) to 20 (Alpinist). On top, you add graphic posts, reels, animations, and stories as individual units. We build a custom bundle based on your actual goals.": "E099", "Do I need to provide my own content?": "E100", "No. We handle everything from strategy to shoot to scheduling. If you have existing assets, great, we'll integrate them. If not, our Still & Motion team produces all the content you need.": "E101", "Can you manage my paid ads as well?": "E102", "Yes. We handle campaign setup and ongoing management including strategy, creative, optimization, and monthly reporting. Up to 3 ad variants with A/B testing.": "E103", "What platforms do you manage?": "E104", "Instagram, Facebook, LinkedIn, and TikTok. Content is formatted per platform: stories, reels, feed posts, carousels, and articles, each sized and optimized for where your audience lives.": "E105", "How fast can you turn around content?": "E106", "Standard turnaround is within the monthly production cycle. Priority, Rush, and Emergency timelines available for accelerated delivery.": "E107", "What does the monthly report include?": "E108", "KPIs, engagement rates, follower growth, top-performing posts, competitor benchmark, audience demographics, and strategic recommendations for the next month.": "E109", "Still Frames That Hold Attention. Moving Images That Move People.": "E110", "Photography, videography, animation, and post-production, handled by a full in-house team that plans, shoots, edits, and delivers production-ready content. Every frame intentional. Every second earned.": "E111", "Start a Production Project": "E112", "What Professional Production Delivers?": "E113", "Our Still & Motion Capabilities": "E114", "How We Run Production": "E115", "Why Brands Choose BoldCrest for Production": "E116", "Content That Matches Your Brand's Ambition — Your audience judges quality in the first second. Professionally shot, edited, and graded content instantly signals that your brand is serious, polished, and worth paying attention to.": "E117", "A Full Visual Library — One production day with our team generates months of content: feed photos, reels, product shots, stories, and animation assets, all from a single coordinated session.": "E118", "Consistent Quality at Scale — Whether it's your 3rd shoot or your 30th, the same creative directors, photographers, and editors maintain your brand's visual standard across every frame.": "E119", "Photography — Content shoots, editorial sessions, product photography, food styling, event coverage, and lifestyle campaigns. Our in-house team delivers 10-40 retouched images per session.": "E120", "Videography — From scripted TVC spots to raw behind-the-scenes content, we handle pre-production, on-set direction, and multi-camera capture. Reels priced by complexity and delivery method.": "E121", "Animation — GIFs, animated social posts, motion graphics, and full animation reels. From simple text reveals to complex product showcases to animated TVCs. Experience across 31 clients.": "E122", "Motion Graphics — Campaign teasers, branded intro sequences, data visualizations, and animated explainers. 2D and 2.5D motion work for social, digital screens, events, and broadcast.": "E123", "Post-Production — Editing, assembly, transitions, audio sync, sound design, and final mastering. We turn raw material into polished, platform-ready content.": "E124", "Color Grading — Professional color correction and grading that gives your footage a distinctive, consistent visual signature. From simple correction to cinematic-grade looks.": "E125", "Pre-Production & Planning — We define the shot list, scout locations, plan logistics, and assemble the right team. Every production day is meticulously planned for maximum output.": "E126", "Creative Direction — Our creative directors are on-set, guiding every frame. Composition, lighting, talent direction, and brand alignment are managed in real-time, not fixed in post.": "E127", "Capture — Photography and video captured by our in-house team: 2-6 people per shoot depending on scope. Photographers, videographers, coordinators, and account managers.": "E128", "Editing & Post-Production — Raw footage becomes polished content: cutting, transitions, audio, color grading, and platform formatting. Animation and motion graphics crafted frame by frame.": "E129", "Retouching & Finishing — Images retouched by our specialist retouchers. Basic retouching for content shoots, advanced retouching for editorial and beauty work, and product cutouts for e-commerce.": "E130", "Delivery & Asset Management — Final files delivered in all required formats and resolutions. Platform-specific exports for social, web, and print. Organized asset library so nothing gets lost.": "E131", "Full In-House Team — Key photographers, dedicated retouchers, video editors, and animators. No outsourcing roulette. The same people who know your brand shoot and edit your content.": "E132", "Extensive Photoshoot Experience — Across 15 clients. From half-day content sessions to multi-day editorial campaigns, we've handled productions of every scale.": "E133", "Batch Efficiency — A Batch Shoot (4+ reels) costs 30-40% less per reel than solo sessions. We plan for maximum output per production day.": "E134", "Animation Depth Others Can't Match — 31 clients served. Style consistency across your entire content ecosystem.": "E135", "Pricing Built From Real Work — Every price in our catalog is built from real project data, not industry benchmarks. You know exactly what you're paying for.": "E136", "Editorial-Grade When You Need It — Fashion-grade, campaign-quality imagery when the brief demands the highest tier of production.": "E137", "What happens on a typical production day?": "E138", "Our team (3-6 people depending on scope) arrives with a locked shot list, all equipment, and a creative director managing every frame. A half-day session delivers 10-15 retouched images; a full day delivers 20-30+ images plus potential reel footage.": "E139", "Can I book just photography, or do I need a full retainer?": "E140", "Photography is available as a one-time project or as a monthly add-on. You can also add regular photo shoots as an add-on to a social media retainer for consistent content flow.": "E141", "What types of animation do you offer?": "E142", "We offer everything from simple GIFs and animated posts through standard motion graphics and complex product showcases to full animation reels and project-level motion graphics. Pricing scales with complexity and length.": "E143", "Do you handle TVC production?": "E144", "Yes. We handle animated TVCs end-to-end: concept, storyboard, animation, sound design, and color. For live-action TVCs, we manage the full production: scripting, talent, shooting, editing, and post.": "E145", "How fast can you deliver edited content?": "E146", "Founder": "F001", "Production Lead": "F002", "Head of Operations": "F003", "Copy & Media Manager": "F004", "Account Manager": "F005", "Still & Motion Coordinator": "F006", "Office & Set Manager": "F007", "Graphic Designer": "F008", "Still & Motion Executive": "F009", "Head of Finance": "F010", "Senior Accountant": "F011", "Digital Marketing Specialist": "F012", "Content Creator": "F013", "Worm Analyst": "F014", "Woof Specialist": "F015", "Build identities and shape perceptions.": "A001", "Go bold or go unseen.": "A002", "identities": "A003", "perceptions": "A004", "bold": "A005", "unseen": "A006", "We do many ⟦View All Work⟧ things very well.": "A007", "No egos, just ⟦The Team⟧ behind the bold.": "A008", "No egos, just the team behind the bold.": "A009", "Let's have ⟦A Coffee⟧ together.": "A010", "Two earthquakes, a pandemic, and a decision.": "A011", "The equation was simple, but powerful. Creative vision on one side. Business understanding on the other. Together, they became the foundation for what BoldCrest would grow into. We were 22, building our first team from the same university halls we were still walking through, driven by clear instinct, strong work ethic, and the belief that the market was ready for something sharper.": "A012", "The work we're most proud of, most people will never know we made.": "A013", "That's not false modesty. That's the goal. When a brand becomes so real, so lived-in, so theirs; when people carry it, wear it, post it, and believe in it without a second thought; the agency behind it disappears. And it should.": "A014"